(2) Yama told Śaśabindu (13. 89. 1) that by offering a kāmya śrāddha under Citrā one got handsome sons 13. 89. 7.

B. Bad omens:

(1) Karṇa pointed out to Kṛṣṇa that the Kauravas were facing great danger because the planet (Mahāpāta) was severely afflicting Citrā (nūnaṁ mahad bhayaṁ kṛṣṇa kurūṇāṁ samupasthitam/ viśeṣeṇa hi vārṣṇeya citrāṁ pīḍayate grahaḥ//) 5. 141. 9 (Nī. on Bom.
